{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17827 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate is implicated in the biological activity of HCC1937 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that this compound targets dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases, which in turn are targeted by Javanicoside F and 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine. These kinases are likely involved in signaling pathways that regulate cellular processes critical to the transformation of HCC1937, potentially influencing its malignant properties. The integration of these targets highlights a complex network of molecular interactions, where Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate may exert its effects through the modulation of these kinases, which are central to the progression of the disease. The presence of multiple pathways converging on HCC1937 underscores the importance of these kinases in the context of the compound's biological activity.",
